1
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:12,900
Come and take a look, won't you?

2
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:28,420
Like someone calling out to me,
after the rain stopped.

3
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
led by the hand of Gaaja.

4
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,420
Hey, that strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:47,720
So, on the arcade guide tiles,

6
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:53,480
I walked only on the black parts.

7
00:00:56,280 --> 00:01:01,780
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

8
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:09,080
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow above their eyes too.

9
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:14,660
Try turning that corner over there.

10
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,900
You can meet everyone, everyone.

11
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:27,800
There's a turtle there
(Kame-ari). Surely there's a turtle.

12
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:33,060
Everyone, come on over to our town.

13
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:34,560
Thank you.

14
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,380
Run, Kameari King-Oh!

15
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:45,020
The horses round the fourth corner
and enter the final straight.

16
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:46,360
Nerima Gallop leads the field.

17
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:47,680
Nerima Gallop is pulling away.

18
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:49,620
Fuji TV Gin comes from the outside!

19
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:50,800
Can Nerima Gallop hold on?

20
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:51,540
Fuji TV Gin!

21
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:52,220
Fuji TV Gin!

22
00:01:52,220 --> 00:01:53,180
Fuji TV Gin!

23
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:53,940
It's pulled clear!

24
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,660
The winner is Fuji TV Gin!

25
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:07,440
In an instant, this month's salary is gone!

26
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:14,840
Could there be a winning ticket among these?

27
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:27,260
Wow, I look so picturesque that

28
00:02:28,820 --> 00:02:29,880
you idiot!

29
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,880
What a pitiful sight this is.

30
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:35,160
For a police officer, it's so shameful.

31
00:02:35,580 --> 00:02:38,120
But police officers are human too,

32
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:42,160
and our salaries are nothing
compared to politicians'.

33
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:45,840
Isn't there any need to
compare us to politicians?

34
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:46,640
That's right.

35
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:51,380
Nakagawa and Reiko never want for money,
so they can say that.

36
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:55,000
People like me, every month,
starting two weeks before payday,

37
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,040
try living on nothing but cup noodles!

38
00:02:58,040 --> 00:03:02,620
It's only natural to work hard to
add even one yen to our meager funds.

39
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:06,400
Then don't rely on gambling like
horse racing or bicycle racing,

40
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:08,840
and just save your money steadily instead.

41
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,500
Chief, you say that,

42
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:15,520
but saving diligently with no purpose at all

43
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:17,280
just isn't my style.

44
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:20,220
Then you should find some goal to aim for.

45
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:23,400
Like saving up for a wedding fund,

46
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,900
or buying a car,

47
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:27,240
or owning a home, too.

48
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:30,860
Wedding? Car? Home?

49
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:32,860
Ugh, no thanks.

50
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:35,960
Saving money for something so dreamless?

51
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:37,480
What are you talking about?

52
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:41,240
Marriage, a car,
and a home are all noble dreams!

53
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:45,380
Those are just the kind of dreams people with a play-it-safe,
sacrifice-bunt mindset have,

54
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:47,660
the sort of dreams
ordinary common folk have.

55
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:52,980
You need a bigger, grander dream
that truly stirs a man's heart.

56
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:56,360
Honestly,
you always have a comeback for everything.

57
00:03:58,040 --> 00:04:02,340
Anyway, I absolutely won't let
you borrow against your salary.

58
00:04:02,340 --> 00:04:04,680
You'll have to figure it out yourself.

59
00:04:05,740 --> 00:04:06,180
Hmph.

60
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:10,060
This is really like
preaching to a horse's ear.

61
00:04:10,060 --> 00:04:10,640
Yeah, right.

62
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:23,180
When you have no money,
it's best to go to bed early.

63
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:27,080
Tonight's guest is the owner whose horse
won the Ochiba Memorial the other day,

64
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:30,900
the owner of Fuji TV Gin, Mr. Umanari To.

65
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:35,380
If only Fuji TV Gin hadn't shown up back then,
by now...

66
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:41,980
So, Mr. Umanari,
I hear you own over a hundred racehorses,

67
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:47,960
and with your latest Fuji TV Gin win, your total
prize money has reportedly topped 5 billion yen.

68
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:49,560
5 billion yen.

69
00:04:51,340 --> 00:04:54,760
For me,
how much I've earned doesn't matter at all.

70
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:57,340
Becoming a racehorse owner and winning.

71
00:04:57,340 --> 00:05:00,380
I believe that's a man's true romance.

72
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:01,580
That's it!

73
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:05,280
No matter how big a long shot you hit at the races,
it's small potatoes.

74
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:10,460
Becoming a horse's owner makes you far
more money for sure than betting on horses.

75
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:13,720
I never noticed such a simple thing!

76
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,260
I'm doing it!

77
00:05:15,260 --> 00:05:18,000
I'm going to become a racehorse owner.

78
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:22,300
You're buying a horse?

79
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:24,680
Look at that glossy coat,

80
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:26,040
and those supple legs.

81
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:29,560
This one will soon become a famous
horse that outshines Fuji TV Gin.

82
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,560
My eye is never wrong.

83
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,900
That's why I'm saving money.

84
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:35,720
Are you serious, senpai?

85
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:37,820
Dead serious. Super serious.

86
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:41,460
To save money,
I'm keeping my food budget to 100 yen a day.

87
00:05:41,980 --> 00:05:43,780
So that's why you look so gaunt.

88
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:45,820
You'll end up with malnutrition.

89
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:48,840
So how much does this horse cost?

90
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:50,760
It's 18 million yen.

91
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:52,560
18 million yen?

92
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:55,900
So how much have you saved so far?

93
00:05:55,900 --> 00:06:00,280
As of yesterday, 8,790 yen.

94
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:04,560
That leaves 17,991,210 yen to go.

95
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:08,860
I've got a headache.

96
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:11,960
Senpai, shouldn't you avoid overdoing it?

97
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:14,740
That's right. You should save up slowly.

98
00:06:14,740 --> 00:06:15,680
Shut up.

99
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:18,520
Are you trying to pick
holes in my savings plan?

100
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:20,340
No, I didn't mean it like that.

101
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:23,500
With my buy-and-sell savings method,

102
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:26,960
I'll have 18 million yen
saved in just ten days!

103
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:30,720
No way, 18 million yen in ten days?

104
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:32,140
Unbelievable.

105
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:34,460
Ignorant fools.

106
00:06:34,460 --> 00:06:36,520
Very well, let me explain.

107
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,880
My buy-and-sell savings method is

108
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:41,420
Tomorrow, I save double what I saved today.

109
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:44,600
For example, on day one,
we start with 10 yen.

110
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:46,180
The next day, 20 yen.

111
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:49,460
And the day after that,
40 yen, doubling each day.

112
00:06:50,740 --> 00:06:53,440
This way, saving is effortless.

113
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:56,660
Look at this chart.

114
00:06:57,260 --> 00:07:01,320
As of yesterday,
I've already saved 8,790 yen.

115
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:05,020
By my calculation,
in ten days it'll be 18 million yen.

116
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:08,260
In a way, yeah.

117
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:10,860
Surprised Chief?

118
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:13,060
Please don't tell anyone, okay?

119
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:15,580
This savings method is my patent, so

120
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:17,400
You really are something else.

121
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:19,860
Do you really think it'll actually build up?

122
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:21,920
Nine million yen on the tenth day?

123
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,700
Where's he planning to get that from?

124
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:25,980
Leave him be.
I've had enough, I'm done with it.

125
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:30,100
The day I become this horse's owner is coming soon,
you know.

126
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:31,980
I've even thought up a name for it.

127
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:34,160
It's Kame-ari King

128
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:36,520
Sounds strong, doesn't it?

129
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:42,400
Does he not realize that "King
" and "Oh" both mean king?

130
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:43,480
Probably not.

131
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,080
That's strange.

132
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:53,400
Suddenly, saving has gotten really tough.

133
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:55,960
According to my calculations,
it shouldn't be unreasonable,

134
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:59,020
though I did expect it
to get a little tough.

135
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:01,460
Let me calculate it once more.

136
00:08:03,340 --> 00:08:04,520
Yep, it's correct.

137
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:05,940
Why is that?

138
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:09,000
Don't tell me there's something
unreasonable somewhere in the plan.

139
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:12,080
Kameari Kongō!

140
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:13,920
Kameari Kongō wins!

141
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:16,200
Champion, Kameari Kongō!

142
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:19,180
Strong Hachiku's seven straight wins!

143
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:21,120
takes the Derby!

144
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:26,240
I won't give up!

145
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:28,920
A man's dream: five billion yen!

146
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:32,520
Senpai did?

147
00:08:32,860 --> 00:08:33,800
That's right.

148
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:37,200
He's been putting fire tools and treasures
up for auction one after another,

149
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:39,160
and apparently selling them off too.

150
00:08:39,160 --> 00:08:41,700
Good morning, everyone.

151
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:47,500
Ryotsu, what's wrong?

152
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:49,780
What's wrong with me?

153
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:51,800
You look pale.

154
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:53,840
What kind of life are you living, anyway?

155
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,420
What do you mean?

156
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:58,380
I'm living on five yen a day.

157
00:08:58,920 --> 00:08:59,060
Five yen?

158
00:08:59,300 --> 00:09:01,380
Is there anything you
can even buy for five yen?

159
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:08,160
I bought a bag of biscuits for 210 yen,
tax included.

160
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:11,940
When I counted, there were 31 in it.

161
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:16,080
At one and a half a day,
that comes to five yen.

162
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:22,480
Other than that,
all I eat is water and grass.

163
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:23,220
Grass?

164
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:25,960
Plantain and shepherd's purse,
and stuff like that.

165
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:30,200
Are you a rabbit?
Why do you do such a stupid thing?

166
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:35,500
With all due respect, Chief, you're the
one who said to save money with a purpose.

167
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:37,720
Well, that's true.

168
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:41,620
So you still haven't given up
on becoming a racehorse owner?

169
00:09:42,460 --> 00:09:43,700
Of course not.

170
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:47,420
No matter what, I'll own a horse of my own.

171
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:52,980
Well, I'm off on a real patrol,
not a can-collecting one.

172
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:55,480
Is Ryo-chan going to be okay?

173
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:57,220
He's going to get sick, isn't he?

174
00:09:57,220 --> 00:09:59,680
He's tougher than a cockroach.

175
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:01,580
No need to worry about that.

176
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:11,260
Lately it's all just plastic bottles,

177
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:13,880
and there are fewer glass
bottles and cans that make money.

178
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:19,700
Ice cream winning sticks!

179
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:22,780
Let's sell them to the kids at half price.

180
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:26,000
Is there anything else?

181
00:10:30,060 --> 00:10:31,140
No good.

182
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:32,320
Why?

183
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:34,700
No matter what, I keep hitting a dead end.

184
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:37,740
The Ryotsu-style buy-and-sell
savings plan has failed.

185
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:38,940
Why is this happening?

186
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:41,840
It was supposed to be a perfect plan.

187
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:42,520
Damn it.

188
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,660
Only eight more times to go!

189
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:45,100
Damn it.

190
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:45,840
Damn it.

191
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:47,160
Senpai...

192
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:49,500
Please don't be so discouraged.

193
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:52,020
Senpai...

194
00:10:53,780 --> 00:10:57,120
Nothing to lose!
With this money, I'll become a Bulgy!

195
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:02,800
What, that horse has been sold?

196
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:06,400
Someone came by yesterday
insisting they had to have it.

197
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:08,580
Damn, I was one step too late.

198
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:10,540
That's too bad.

199
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:14,560
Old man, I want that horse for 36,000 yen.

200
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:21,520
What, 36,000 yen? Are you serious? You
think you can buy a racehorse for 36,000 yen?

201
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:24,040
I'm serious. Look me in the eye.

202
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:30,740
Alright, I like your bold,
no-nonsense attitude.

203
00:11:30,740 --> 00:11:32,440
I'll sell it to you for 36,000.

204
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:33,560
Really?

205
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:40,420
This one is a half-brother of that horse,
with a different mother and a different father.

206
00:11:40,420 --> 00:11:42,640
This one is a top-class champion too.

207
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:46,180
On top of that,
I bought it for the Kameari Kinen.

208
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:49,260
It has the same birthday
as that Fuji TV Gin.

209
00:11:49,260 --> 00:11:50,440
Looks fast, doesn't it?

210
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:54,580
Since he's that horse's brother,
I'm an owner now too.

211
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:02,963
Senpai, if they have different
mothers and different fathers,

212
00:12:03,013 --> 00:12:06,300
doesn't that make them
completely different horses?

213
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,906
Now that I think about it, I suppose so.

214
00:12:09,956 --> 00:12:12,740
I went and bought it on a whim back then.

215
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:20,580
Is this really a racehorse?

216
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:23,680
Its legs are short, and it's plump all over.

217
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:26,420
Damn it, that old man tricked me!

218
00:12:29,260 --> 00:12:30,680
Did it already eat all of that?

219
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:32,220
It really eats a lot, doesn't it?

220
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:34,120
It's asking for seconds.

221
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,440
No, no, no way.

222
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:38,520
Come on! Training starts now
so we can earn five billion yen!

223
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:47,080
You went and did it, didn't you?

224
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:50,120
Reiko, get out of the way!

225
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:52,660
Ryo-chan, you should forgive it.

226
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:54,280
I didn't do it on purpose.

227
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:56,980
You're a slick one, aren't you?

228
00:13:15,380 --> 00:13:17,700
Listen, the race is decided at the start!

229
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:19,740
If you get off to a slow start,
it's all over.

230
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:20,760
So,

231
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:27,020
Don't go listening to Morning Musume or whatever,
you little brat!

232
00:13:27,020 --> 00:13:28,060
You bastard!

233
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:30,740
You start the moment the gate opens!

234
00:13:30,740 --> 00:13:31,420
Got it?

235
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:34,200
Alright then,

236
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:35,660
Good, that's it!

237
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:40,620
Idiot, watch the front!

238
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,000
This guy

239
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:58,040
You did that on purpose, didn't you

240
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:00,200
Seriously?

241
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:05,340
Alright, I'll let you off just this once.

242
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:08,100
What a cocky one you are.

243
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:10,060
This place isn't good.

244
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:11,860
Let's go somewhere else
and continue the training.

245
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:14,940
Here, the ground under our feet is dirt, so

246
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:17,600
we won't have to worry about injuries,
and we can practice properly.

247
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:21,780
Listen up. I'm the one they call
the Hoshi Ittetsu of the racing world.

248
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:23,460
I'm going to train you thoroughly.

249
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:28,400
You're going to become the
star of Nakayama Racecourse.

250
00:14:30,780 --> 00:14:31,520
Good,

251
00:14:31,570 --> 00:14:36,580
you're going to sprint at full
speed to that signpost over there.

252
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:37,960
Got it?

253
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:40,980
Here we go, ready...

254
00:14:40,980 --> 00:14:42,680
Go!

255
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:48,400
Shift your weight onto
your forelegs quickly.

256
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:50,580
Push up powerfully with your hind legs.

257
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:52,320
Just a little more!

258
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,120
Keep it up!

259
00:14:58,700 --> 00:14:59,920
Hey, that one there,

260
00:15:01,140 --> 00:15:03,380
to be outrun this badly by a human?

261
00:15:03,380 --> 00:15:04,460
What kind of horse are you?

262
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:09,040
Do you even have any motivation?

263
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:11,620
What?

264
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:16,280
What's wrong? Are you too hungry to run?

265
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:20,560
Then just eat some of the grass over there.

266
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:24,780
What? You're a horse,
and you won't eat grass?

267
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:30,140
You want ramen instead?

268
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:36,160
Welcome!

269
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:38,300
One ramen, please.

270
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:40,640
The horse talked!

271
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:43,260
Horse, horse, horse!

272
00:15:43,260 --> 00:15:45,820
It wasn't the horse, it was me.

273
00:15:46,860 --> 00:15:48,760
It's just Ryo-san.

274
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:50,420
Don't scare us like that.

275
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:55,380
If the horse could talk, I'd make
him a comedian instead of a racehorse.

276
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:57,760
Make him a bowl of ramen.

277
00:15:57,760 --> 00:15:59,740
A horse eating ramen?

278
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:02,700
These days, anything goes.

279
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:04,680
What?

280
00:16:04,680 --> 00:16:05,360
What?

281
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:11,100
Don't make the soup too hot.

282
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:13,460
For a horse, you've got a sensitive tongue

283
00:16:13,460 --> 00:16:14,840
Do you want the noodles firm?

284
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:16,920
Coming right up.

285
00:16:16,920 --> 00:16:19,700
I never thought a horse
would come in for ramen.

286
00:16:19,700 --> 00:16:21,320
What a terrible age we live in.

287
00:16:21,860 --> 00:16:22,820
Here you go, sorry for the wait.

288
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:24,680
Thanks.

289
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:28,880
What's wrong? Eat up already.

290
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:30,900
What?

291
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,020
Pepper?

292
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:35,800
Here you go.

293
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,620
What kind of diet are you on, anyway?

294
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:46,880
There, I've fed you,
so this time you'd better run perfectly.

295
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:51,160
Alright, take your positions... get set...

296
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:55,900
Who told you to sleep?

297
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:00,600
Don't sleep, run!

298
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:03,080
This isn't nap time at kindergarten,
you know.

299
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:07,580
If you don't plan on running,
I'll give you a whipping.

300
00:17:08,980 --> 00:17:12,120
At this rate,
it's like I'm the one being trained.

301
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:15,040
It's a horse.

302
00:17:15,040 --> 00:17:16,100
It's the real thing.

303
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:18,580
Ryo-san.

304
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:22,880
Ryo-san, let me ride that horse.

305
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:23,800
Let me ride.

306
00:17:23,800 --> 00:17:24,920
Come on, let us ride it.

307
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:26,260
No way, no way.

308
00:17:26,260 --> 00:17:29,380
This horse is in special
training to become a racehorse.

309
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:32,320
I don't have time to play around with kids.

310
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:34,100
Come on, let us ride it.

311
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:37,700
That's right, if you don't get out, I'll
tell the Chief you were slacking off again!

312
00:17:37,700 --> 00:17:40,780
Are these guys trying to
intimidate a police officer's legs?

313
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:43,680
What, you'll let us ride it?

314
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:46,940
Wow, this is the best one?

315
00:17:47,060 --> 00:17:47,720
This is it!

316
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:49,340
Come on, come on, take turns, take turns.

317
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:54,880
Stop it!

318
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:55,060
Quit it!

319
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:59,640
Hahaha

320
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:04,400
He really suits playing with kids the most,
doesn't he.

321
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:05,760
Huh!

322
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:09,580
Don't joke around!
I've put a lot of capital into that thing!

323
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:13,140
I'm going to train you into
a racehorse no matter what!

324
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,180
Run!

325
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:23,420
One, two, one, two!

326
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,720
What's the matter? You two?

327
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:33,160
I've already given up.

328
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:36,600
Are you trying to make
this horse a racehorse?

329
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:39,683
Look, this guy's just a big eater,

330
00:18:39,733 --> 00:18:41,620
and he won't run at all.

331
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:44,880
We've finally run out of food
and money since yesterday.

332
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:48,820
So what are you going to do with this horse?
Are you getting rid of him?

333
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,980
Nobody will buy him.

334
00:18:50,980 --> 00:18:52,540
Then what are we going to do?

335
00:18:52,540 --> 00:18:56,080
Anyway, I'll go look for a
part-time job this guy can do.

336
00:18:58,620 --> 00:19:01,917
Alright, the protagonist is going to hop
on the horse and go for a run right away!

337
00:19:01,967 --> 00:19:02,880
Let's go see.

338
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:04,840
And now, the real start!

339
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:14,160
You're fired!

340
00:19:18,380 --> 00:19:20,360
After all that trouble
getting you a part-time job!

341
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:23,380
Do you even want to work or not?

342
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:28,860
What? Running just isn't your style?

343
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:32,140
This one's probably not
cut out to be a racehorse.

344
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:37,960
Living together,
I've come to understand this horse.

345
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:42,860
If the part-time job won't work,
we'll make a field here and harvest crops.

346
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:48,080
What? Farm work goes against
a thoroughbred's pride?

347
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:52,380
Besides, I'm no good with earthworms.

348
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:57,420
Do you want to be sold
to the butcher that badly?

349
00:19:58,260 --> 00:20:00,500
Then stop complaining and plow!

350
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:04,940
Stop dawdling and get started!

351
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:10,280
Good, that's it.

352
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:18,840
What? You want to take a break?

353
00:20:19,280 --> 00:20:22,660
You idiot,
you haven't even gone a single meter!

354
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:27,000
I don't care about you anymore.

355
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:29,200
I'll take care of it while you sleep.

356
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:31,080
Go get picked up by whoever you like.

357
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:34,420
Shut up.

358
00:20:35,300 --> 00:20:36,640
No matter what you say, it's not happening.

359
00:20:52,740 --> 00:20:53,800
I'll be right back.

360
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:55,220
Behave yourself, okay?

361
00:20:55,220 --> 00:20:56,020
Okay~

362
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:13,000
Somebody!

363
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,840
Somebody, help!

364
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:22,900
This is bad! A car fell in!

365
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:26,540
Satoru-chan, help!
There's a child in the car!

366
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:27,920
Ohhhhhh!

367
00:21:28,900 --> 00:21:31,300
Aaaaaaah!

368
00:21:31,300 --> 00:21:34,200
It's sinking!

369
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:39,640
Alright, I'll save them now!

370
00:21:39,640 --> 00:21:43,140
Eeeeeeeh!

371
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:45,400
Eeeeeeeh!

372
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:50,020
No good,
I'm too hungry to put any strength into it!

373
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:52,760
Aaaaaaah!

374
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:54,920
Exxxxar!

375
00:22:10,420 --> 00:22:12,720
King-Oh!

376
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:19,420
Pull back!

377
00:22:23,760 --> 00:22:25,000
Eeeeeeeh!

378
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:33,080
Hang in there, just a little more!

379
00:22:46,460 --> 00:22:47,420
We did it!

380
00:22:47,420 --> 00:22:48,640
Satoru-chan!

381
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:50,160
Satoru-chan!

382
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:54,380
King-Oh!

383
00:22:55,740 --> 00:22:58,560
The two of us saved that child's life!

384
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:01,460
King-Oh!

385
00:23:02,700 --> 00:23:04,020
Sorry about earlier.

386
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:07,580
No matter what happens,
I'm never letting you go.

387
00:23:12,440 --> 00:23:13,240
Excuse me.

388
00:23:13,240 --> 00:23:17,760
We've had the pleasure
of seeing your exploits.

389
00:23:17,760 --> 00:23:19,480
You flatter us.

390
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:24,120
My master says he's taken
a real liking to that horse.

391
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:29,220
He'd very much like to buy it from you.

392
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:33,840
What do you say?

393
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:38,240
No matter how much money you offer,
I won't hand this one over.

394
00:23:38,240 --> 00:23:41,800
King O and I are one body and soul,
now and forever.

395
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:42,500
Right?

396
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:53,840
This confession

397
00:23:54,380 --> 00:23:57,960
What was that refreshing
feeling from just now?

398
00:24:00,860 --> 00:24:05,520
I kicked the alarm clock and stubbed my pinky toe,
ouch ouch!

399
00:24:07,300 --> 00:24:13,880
Once I've drawn my eyebrows, it's dance,
dance, dance all the way to the station

400
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:19,340
Packed train, sleeping on Dad's back, surely

401
00:24:20,520 --> 00:24:25,680
Hard work again this week, and your
unreasonable demands are perfectly reasonable

402
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:33,340
Looking cool with a bucket in hand, but
it's beef bowl with extra soggy, extra sauce

403
00:24:33,340 --> 00:24:40,220
Overtime-streak irritation,
neatly cleared away by more irritation

404
00:24:43,540 --> 00:24:50,000
Every day's no problem,
once I've passed through a hot shower

405
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:56,560
Every day's no problem,
my energy restored by a sleep pillow

406
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:06,160
Every day's no problem,
I love a girl like me

407
00:25:06,160 --> 00:25:12,920
Every day's no problem,
hearts flying on a Monday

408
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:24,620
What? My painting won the gold
prize at the art exhibition?

409
00:25:25,140 --> 00:25:26,360
That's right, that's right.

410
00:25:26,360 --> 00:25:29,040
After all,
those who truly see it will understand.

411
00:25:29,420 --> 00:25:30,700
Besides, Chief

412
00:25:30,700 --> 00:25:34,100
How dare you call my painting a doodle!

413
00:25:34,520 --> 00:25:36,860
Next time: the genius painter appears!

414
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:37,920
Nice to meet you.

415
00:25:45,260 --> 00:25:49,120
Everyone, come on over to our town!

416
00:25:50,040 --> 00:25:50,680
Thank you.

